# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
# QS-VC Environment Configuration
# Copy to .env and fill in values
# ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# General
NODE_ENV=development

# SFU Service
SFU_PORT=4000
SFU_ANNOUNCED_IP=127.0.0.1
SFU_MIN_PORT=40000
SFU_MAX_PORT=40100
SFU_NUM_WORKERS=2
SFU_LOG_LEVEL=debug

# Signaling Service
SIGNALING_PORT=4001
SIGNALING_SFU_URL=http://localhost:4000

# Auth Service
AUTH_PORT=4002
JWT_SECRET=dev-jwt-secret-change-in-production
JWT_EXPIRY=24h

# Payments (disabled by default). Keep provider secrets server-side; never use VITE_ prefixes.
PAYMENTS_ENABLED=true
PAYMENT_TERMS_CONFIRMED=true
PAYMENT_RETURN_URL=https://qsvcmeet.com
AUTH_PUBLIC_URL=https://qsvcmeet.com
RAZORPAY_KEY_ID=
RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_STARTER=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_PRO=
PAYPAL_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
PAYPAL_WEBHOOK_ID=
PAYPAL_PLAN_STARTER=
PAYPAL_PLAN_PRO=
PAYPAL_CURRENCY=USD
PAYPAL_STARTER_BASE_AMOUNT=
PAYPAL_PRO_BASE_AMOUNT=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_BASIC=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BASIC=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BASIC_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_BASIC_BASE_AMOUNT=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_BASIC_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BASIC_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BASIC_ANNUAL_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_BASIC_ANNUAL_BASE_AMOUNT=
PAYPAL_PLAN_STARTER_TRIAL_14=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_STARTER_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_STARTER_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_STARTER_ANNUAL_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_STARTER_ANNUAL_BASE_AMOUNT=
PAYPAL_PLAN_PRO_TRIAL_14=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_PRO_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_PRO_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_PRO_ANNUAL_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_PRO_ANNUAL_BASE_AMOUNT=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_BUSINESS=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BUSINESS=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BUSINESS_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_BUSINESS_BASE_AMOUNT=
RAZORPAY_PLAN_BUSINESS_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BUSINESS_ANNUAL=
PAYPAL_PLAN_BUSINESS_ANNUAL_TRIAL_14=
PAYPAL_BUSINESS_ANNUAL_BASE_AMOUNT=
CASHFREE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
CASHFREE_API_VERSION=2026-01-01
CASHFREE_CLIENT_ID=
CASHFREE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Optional override. If empty, webhook verification uses CASHFREE_CLIENT_SECRET.
CASHFREE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=

# Meeting Service
MEETING_PORT=4003
WEB_URL=http://localhost:5173

# Recording Service
RECORDING_PORT=4004

# Web Client
VITE_SIGNALING_URL=ws://localhost:4001/ws
VITE_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4002
VITE_MEETING_URL=http://localhost:4003
VITE_RECORDING_URL=http://localhost:4004
VITE_APP_NAME=QS-VC

# PostgreSQL
POSTGRES_HOST=localhost
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DB=qsvc
POSTGRES_USER=qsvc
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=qsvc_dev_2025

# Redis
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379

# MinIO (S3-compatible)
MINIO_ENDPOINT=localhost
MINIO_PORT=9000
MINIO_ACCESS_KEY=qsvc_minio
MINIO_SECRET_KEY=qsvc_minio_secret
MINIO_BUCKET=qsvc-recordings

# TURN/STUN
TURN_SECRET=dev-turn-secret-change-in-production
TURN_SERVERS=turn:backend.qsvcmeet.com:3478?transport=udp,turn:backend.qsvcmeet.com:3478?transport=tcp

# Official Google Cloud Translation (server only; used when CAPTION_TRANSLATION_PROVIDER=google)
# Enable Translation API/billing and restrict this key. Never prefix it with VITE_.
GOOGLE_TRANSLATE_API_KEY=

# Caption translation (signaling, server only). Self-hosted IndicTrans2: run services/mt and set
# LIBRETRANSLATE_URL=http://mt:5000 (it speaks the LibreTranslate API). Or CAPTION_TRANSLATION_PROVIDER=google.
LIBRETRANSLATE_URL=
LIBRETRANSLATE_API_KEY=
CAPTION_TRANSLATION_PROVIDER=google

# Server speech recognition for captions (services/asr). Empty = browser recognition fallback.
ASR_URL=
ASR_API_KEY=
ASR_MAX_SESSIONS=50
# Speech service tuning (services/asr): model, offered languages, words to bias recognition
ASR_MODEL=
# Production: reviewed local bundles, each with qsvc-model-manifest.json.
# Developer downloads require BOTH NODE_ENV=development and this explicit opt-in.
QSVC_ALLOW_UNVERIFIED_MODELS=false
ASR_INDIC_MODEL=/models/indic
MT_MODEL_EN_INDIC=/models/en-indic
MT_MODEL_INDIC_EN=/models/indic-en
ASR_LANGUAGES=hi,en,bn,ta,te,mr,gu,kn,ml,pa,ur,or,as,ne
ASR_PROMPT=QS-VC, UPSWAN, UPDESCO
# Engines: hybrid = Whisper (English/Hindi/Hinglish) + AI4Bharat IndicConformer (other Indian languages)
ASR_ENGINE=hybrid
# Languages routed to IndicConformer (empty = all 22 except Hindi)
ASR_INDIC_LANGUAGES=
# Hugging Face read token: IndicConformer is gated (accept its terms once on huggingface.co)
HF_TOKEN=
MT_LANGUAGES=

# Caption limits (defaults shown)
CAPTION_MAX_ROOMS=500
CAPTION_ROOM_CONCURRENCY=8
CAPTION_GLOBAL_CONCURRENCY=64
CAPTION_PEER_TRANSLATIONS_PER_MINUTE=240
CAPTION_PUBLISH_INTERVAL_MS=300
CAPTION_INTERIM_INTERVAL_MS=200

# AI meeting minutes: any OpenAI-compatible chat endpoint (vLLM / Ollama on-prem, or a hosted provider)
MINUTES_LLM_URL=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
MINUTES_LLM_MODEL=
MINUTES_LLM_API_KEY=

# Cloud RDS: verify-full plus the AWS RDS CA bundle file.
# Intranet: point POSTGRES_HOST at the organisation's local database.
# POSTGRES_SSL=verify-full
# POSTGRES_CA_FILE=/absolute/path/to/ap-south-1-bundle.pem
# DB_APPLICATION_NAME=qsvc-cloud

# Separate restricted login URLs for hosted services (set privately, never VITE_).
# AUTH_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qs_auth_app:ENCODED_PASSWORD@RDS_ENDPOINT:5432/qsvc
# MEETING_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://qs_meeting_app:ENCODED_PASSWORD@RDS_ENDPOINT:5432/qsvc

# Platform admins (full access to every feature). Comma-separated.
# Required when QSVC_DEPLOYMENT=onprem; defaults to built-in list in cloud/development.
# QSVC_ADMIN_EMAILS=admin@your-domain.internal
# Admin online test workspace (optional, for development/demo).
# QSVC_ADMIN_WORKSPACE_URL=https://meet.your-domain.internal
# Local auth development only; production AWS uses the read-only compose mount.
# ENTERPRISE_WINDOWS_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-Windows-x64.zip
# ENTERPRISE_MACOS_ARM64_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-macOS-arm64.zip
# ENTERPRISE_MACOS_X64_INSTALLER=/absolute/path/to/QS-VC-macOS-x64.zip
# Leave unset. Set to yes only while the platform admins create their accounts, then remove it.
# QSVC_ADMIN_SIGNUP_OPEN=yes

# Production SFU control. Use the same random secret in SFU and signaling.
# SFU_CONTROL_TOKEN=

# Optional enterprise MCU path (FreeSWITCH + drachtio; see deploy/poly-bridge).
# The intranet launcher accepts MCU_ENABLED=true (legacy) or
# POLY_BRIDGE_ENABLED=true and fails fast unless these dependencies are reachable.
# POLY_BRIDGE_ENABLED=false
# MCU_ENABLED=false
# BRIDGE_API_TOKEN=
# FS_ESL_HOST=10.0.0.20
# FS_ESL_PORT=8021
# FS_ESL_PASSWORD=
# DRACHTIO_HOST=10.0.0.20
# DRACHTIO_PORT=9022
# DRACHTIO_SECRET=
# BRIDGE_RTP_ANNOUNCED_IP=<SFU address reachable from FreeSWITCH>

# Enable in both auth and signaling for a private workspace with provisioned accounts.
# QSVC_ENTERPRISE_TERMS_REQUIRED=yes

# Enterprise SSO. Set HTTPS public origins in production and start the Compose sso profile.
QSVC_SSO_ENABLED=false
QSVC_SSO_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:4002
QSVC_SSO_WEB_URL=http://localhost:5173
KEYCLOAK_PUBLIC_URL=http://localhost:8085
KEYCLOAK_PORT=8085
QSVC_KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://localhost:8085/realms/qsvc
# QSVC_KEYCLOAK_INTERNAL_URL=http://keycloak:8080
QSVC_KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=
QSVC_KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
KEYCLOAK_DB_ADMIN_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_ADMIN_PASSWORD
KEYCLOAK_DB_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_DATABASE_PASSWORD
KEYCLOAK_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME=qsvc-bootstrap-admin
KEYCLOAK_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=REPLACE_WITH_RANDOM_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD
QSVC_SSO_IDP_HOSTS=

# Optional DigiLocker identity consent. Use endpoints and credentials from your requester account.
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_ENABLED=false
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_AUTHORIZE_URL=
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_TOKEN_URL=
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_USER_URL=
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_ID=
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_CLIENT_SECRET=
QSVC_DIGILOCKER_SCOPE=

# Optional personal sign-in providers. Set these on the auth service only.
QSVC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
QSVC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
QSVC_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=
QSVC_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=
QSVC_EMAIL_API_KEY=
QSVC_EMAIL_FROM=

# Production token keys. Generate with: node scripts/provision-security-keys.mjs
# Only auth receives the private Ed25519 key. Never use a VITE_ prefix for these.
SESSION_SIGNING_KEY_FILE=
INTERNAL_AUTH_SECRET=
TURN_ACCESS_SECRET=
MEETING_POLICY_SECRET=
INVITATION_SECRET=
# Same private value in the AWS proxy and Cloudflare Worker secret binding.
ORIGIN_AUTH_SECRET=
